# Svelte Adapter

- DND-FX.4 is COMPLETE. Keep `@dndgem/svelte` thin; do not add a SvelteKit package, Vue, Angular, or a parallel runtime. Do not reopen Svelte unless an explicit follow-up authorizes it.
- Svelte is a peerDependency of `@dndgem/svelte` (`^5.0.0`). Svelte 4 is not supported.
- Do not bundle Svelte into the library.
- `@dndgem/svelte` may depend on `@dndgem/core` and `@dndgem/dom`.
- Do not place solver, Auto-Layout, provenance, or drag policy in the Svelte package.
- Do not import `@dnd-kit/*`, `@dndgem/react`, `@dndgem/vue`, or `@dndgem/angular` from Svelte. Consume `createLayoutSession` / public DOM types only.
- Host registration uses Svelte actions. Do not add a parallel attachment API unless a later sprint requires it.
- Cleanup must call the DOM session `dispose()` path. Do not invent a parallel Svelte runtime.
- Explicit `desiredPlacements` updates must omit Core `previous` so ADR-0010 stability cannot suppress new author intent (Auto-Layout on keeps `previous` as stability only).
- SvelteKit is a validated compatibility environment (DND-FX.5). Do not create `@dndgem/sveltekit` or a SvelteKit plugin unless a later review proves it is required.
